{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Completion evidence for the two verifier findings: (1) Assertion-parity table — the ticket scope located it in the change description by design; it exists in merged commit 04085bf03 ('Port probe-rebar.sh to Python, assertion parity', git log origin/main --grep 'rebar-ticket: f1eb'), one row per probe section mapping shell assertions to Python: all 140 runtime assertions ported 1:1 by label, 0 retired, +1 gated self-test assertion (PROBE_INJECT_FAIL) = 141 static. Verify: git show 04085bf03 --no-patch. Runtime proof both probes report '140 passed, 0 failed' pre/post port (recorded earlier on this ticket). (2) Shell file presence — scripts/probe-rebar.sh is no longer the probe: it is a 7-line exec shim delegating to scripts/probe_rebar.py, required because gerrit-verify.yaml executes from MAIN's definition (patchset 1 failed golden-path exit 127 without it). All in-tree consumers (test.yml:128, gerrit-verify.yaml:209 golden-path, anti-rot substring in test_probe_wired_into_ci.py, docs/releasing.md) invoke the Python entry point directly; shim deletion is ticket d772-6007-5d04-4101 (discovered_from this ticket), actionable only after this change is in main's workflow definition. Scope line updated to reflect the discovered executes-from-main constraint."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785768528981455001,"uuid":"fdb9c13b-0044-489a-99d8-93ce3b6f57dd"}